WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.156
Years of checkups.

00:00:01.316 --> 00:00:02.237
Different files.

00:00:02.397 --> 00:00:05.193
When you need one old result, the search starts again.

00:00:05.353 --> 00:00:07.281
Modus brings that history around you.

00:00:07.441 --> 00:00:09.265
Every satellite is a real file.

00:00:09.425 --> 00:00:13.254
Open one, and its recorded readings stay connected to the original.

00:00:13.433 --> 00:00:16.395
Ask: when did I last have blood pressure of one hundred?

00:00:16.555 --> 00:00:18.612
Modus first asks which number you mean.

00:00:18.772 --> 00:00:19.924
Choose the top number.

00:00:20.084 --> 00:00:22.110
It finds May fourth, twenty sixteen.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:26.400
Open the answer, and there is the original: one hundred over seventy.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:28.848
The date and evidence are part of the answer.

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:30.536
Now bring in a new report.

00:00:30.696 --> 00:00:35.681
Muse Spark reads the image, checks proposed evidence, and looks again for missing rows.

00:00:35.841 --> 00:00:40.141
It found all three rows here, but left the header date and specimen for review.

00:00:40.301 --> 00:00:42.963
I confirm those from the original before saving.

00:00:43.123 --> 00:00:46.159
The warning stays visible: source checks can miss things.

00:00:46.333 --> 00:00:48.672
Compare that report with an earlier checkup.

00:00:48.832 --> 00:00:54.831
Muse must inspect the selected reports, then check related records within the same captured history.

00:00:54.991 --> 00:00:58.007
Here, two earlier copies both say five point six.

00:00:58.167 --> 00:01:01.624
But one says H P L C, and the other says immunoassay.

00:01:01.784 --> 00:01:02.870
The number matches.

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.642
The recorded method does not.

00:01:04.833 --> 00:01:05.824
Open the finding.

00:01:05.984 --> 00:01:07.709
Both original sources are here.

00:01:07.869 --> 00:01:12.297
Modus explains the recorded difference without deciding which copy is right.

00:01:12.457 --> 00:01:16.619
It also withholds a numerical comparison when the context is uncertain.

00:01:16.779 --> 00:01:20.134
Muse can request bounded reads and select checked findings.

00:01:20.294 --> 00:01:21.763
It cannot rewrite the record.

00:01:21.933 --> 00:01:26.338
If a saved field needs correction, review the exact change before saving it.

00:01:26.498 --> 00:01:30.221
The previous explanation becomes stale and asks for a refresh.

00:01:30.381 --> 00:01:32.338
Your correction becomes a new version.

00:01:32.498 --> 00:01:37.689
The original file, its printed wording, and the earlier saved version remain available.

00:01:37.849 --> 00:01:39.525
Nothing is silently replaced.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:41.903
An old report can arrive years later.

00:01:42.063 --> 00:01:47.234
This result was recorded in twenty nineteen, but its file arrived in twenty twenty-six.

00:01:47.394 --> 00:01:49.082
Today's history can include it.

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:53.673
Replay what was available in twenty twenty-five, and it stays outside that view.

00:01:53.833 --> 00:01:58.023
New evidence changes today's picture without rewriting what was known then.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.216
Behind the interface, Muse reads and investigates.

00:02:01.376 --> 00:02:06.181
Typed tools own comparisons and bind findings to exact records and versions.

00:02:06.341 --> 00:02:09.262
Human-reviewed transactions own every record write.

00:02:09.422 --> 00:02:14.029
Encrypted local storage keeps originals, revisions, and both dates together.

00:02:14.189 --> 00:02:19.441
That is how an answer remains inspectable after files arrive, disagree, or change.

00:02:19.633 --> 00:02:25.174
We tested the investigation on fourteen authored three-report cases using real Muse calls.

00:02:25.334 --> 00:02:31.765
After fixing the comparison rules, it caught all nine expected discrepancies, with zero false flags.

00:02:31.925 --> 00:02:35.274
These are development results, not independent accuracy.

00:02:35.434 --> 00:02:37.422
Take a reviewed summary with its sources.

00:02:37.582 --> 00:02:41.700
Modus Records: find the answer, open the evidence, and keep your history.
